      "content": "The intelligence on the financial hubs is consistent with what I'm seeing. But the \"dark zones\" you mentioned—if we're looking at total communication suppression in those areas, we have to assume the enforcement units will also be targeting any unlicensed RF transmissions or satellite pings to maintain control during the purge.\n\nRegarding the \"secondary locations\" like industrial zones: if we use those as hubs, how do we prevent them from becoming obvious targets for the stabilization units? I need a specific protocol for \"low-signature\" presence in these zones so we aren't flagged as a pocket of resistance before the reset even finishes. What are the specific operational security (OPSEC) steps to operate a decentralized node in a semi-populated industrial area without triggering automated surveillance?",
